DESCRIPTION:In this talk\, I'll delve into my year as an open source intern
  at Pydantic\, offering insights from my experience at a quality-driven\, 
 community-centric company. I'll provide tips for aspiring contributors and
  discuss the value of early career development through open source involve
 ment.
DTSTAMP:20261116T105848Z
LOCATION:Auditorium
SUMMARY:Reflections on My Year as an Open Source Intern at Pydantic - Sydne
 y Runkle
URL:https://pretalx.evolutio.pt/pycon-portugal-2024/talk/PCX3AA/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pretalx-pycon-portugal-2024-S3FCGA@pretalx.evolutio.pt
DTSTART;TZID=WET:20241017T162000
DTEND;TZID=WET:20241017T165000
DESCRIPTION:From the team behind Pydantic\, Logfire is a new type of observ
 ability platform built on the same belief as our open source library — t
 hat the most powerful tools can be easy to use.\n\nIn this talk\, we'll in
 troduce Logfire\, then demonstrate how it can make understanding and fixin
 g your app faster and more enjoyable.\n\nWe'll touch on some of the most u
 seful integrations.
DTSTAMP:20261116T105848Z
LOCATION:Auditorium
SUMMARY:Pydantic Logfire — Uncomplicated Observability - Marcelo Trylesin
 ski\, Sydney Runkle
URL:https://pretalx.evolutio.pt/pycon-portugal-2024/talk/S3FCGA/
